    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p19_b20",
      "text": "First, we provide supplementary analysis using the Informativeness metric from MMHalBench. The MMHalBench score\n(ranging from 0 to 6) is derived from two factors: hallucination status (scores 0\u20132 indicate hallucination, while 3\u20136 indicate\nvalid responses) and information richness (higher scores reflect greater alignment with the ground truth in terms of detail).\nInformativeness serves as a specific metric to quantify the fluency and richness of the model\u2019s output. Formally, it is\n",
